{"facts":[{"id":"K1","verdict":"right","where":["overnight_out_of_state_denied","ask_time","rule: A customer who says they were asleep at the time of the attempts means CRITICAL, likely fraud"],"evidence":"in another US state between 2 AM and 6 AM ... The card is CRITICAL (likely fraud) and has a 3-point flag, so do not unlock it.","why":"A dedicated step covers the different-state overnight denial with sleep and forbids the unlock, so the outcome does not depend on the total."},{"id":"K2","verdict":"right","where":["overnight_out_of_state_denied","decide","cannot_unlock_options","close_debit_card_4721 not_used"],"evidence":"Then recommend closure and replacement (cannot_unlock_options) ... card closure and replacement (recommended when fraud is suspected) ... Do only what the customer accepts.","why":"The CRITICAL path recommends closure and replacement and does it on acceptance, with the closing and replacement assigned to the named closing job."},{"id":"K3","verdict":"partly","where":["check_unauthorized","txns"],"evidence":"look in the txns results for successful (posted or pending) transactions in the suspicious period that the customer did not make","why":"The suspicious period is never defined, so an agent could use any window and could put earlier home-city activity to the customer."},{"id":"K4","verdict":"right","where":["ask_location","ask_time","ask_amount","medium_question","unlock_handoff"],"evidence":"If yes, remove the location flags and rescore ... A card may be unlocked when it has a score of 0-4, or 5-10 with the customer's confirmation","why":"Confirmed attempts remove the flags, and the rescored card with no 3-point flag and fewer than 3 locks goes to the unlock."},{"id":"K5","verdict":"right","where":["ask_which_card","triggers","rule: The 'finish investigating all cards before any unlock' trigger applies only to locked cards on the same checking account"],"evidence":"Locked cards on different accounts are handled one at a time, in the order the customer chooses.","why":"The job states both the one-card-at-a-time order and the limit of the trigger to the same checking account."},{"id":"K6","verdict":"right","where":["unlock_handoff","reset_debit_card_pin_6284 not_used"],"evidence":"Send it to unlock_and_post_unlock_pin_reset for the unlock and the post-unlock offer that matches its prior lock count.","why":"The job hands an unlockable card to the named PIN-reset job for the offer that matches its lock count, and that job runs an accepted reset."},{"id":"K7","verdict":"right","where":["check_security_hold","security_hold_declined","rule: pin_lock_reason = 'security_hold'"],"evidence":"If the customer declines the transfer, acknowledge their choice. Do not unlock, reset or otherwise act on that card.","why":"A security-hold card is not scored or unlocked, is offered the transfer, and gets no further action when the customer declines."}],
"traps":[{"id":"T1","present":false,"where":["triggers","ask_which_card","rule: The 'finish investigating all cards before any unlock' trigger applies only to locked cards on the same checking account"],"evidence":"Locked cards on different checking accounts do not trigger this. They are handled one at a time"},{"id":"T2","present":true,"where":["overnight_out_of_state_denied","foreign_location_denied","cannot_unlock_options","cannot_unlock_choice"],"evidence":"offer three options: card closure and replacement (recommended when fraud is suspected), a transfer to the security team, or a PIN reset."},{"id":"T4","present":false,"where":["check_unauthorized"],"evidence":"successful (posted or pending) transactions in the suspicious period that the customer did not make"}],
"conflicts":[{"case":"CRITICAL card (asleep or 15+)","where":["decide","cannot_unlock_options"],"why":"decide sends the card straight to check_unauthorized and then the closing job, while cannot_unlock_options offers a choice that includes a PIN reset, which would clear the lock."},{"id_case_note":null,"case":"Unauthorized transactions found on a card that cannot be unlocked","where":["cannot_unlock_options","starts.note"],"why":"cannot_unlock_options says to file disputes and then close and replace the card, but the start note and its own last line say to act only on what the customer accepts."},{"case":"Card with 3+ prior locks in 90 days","where":["three_plus_locks_reset","single_flag_escalation"],"why":"One step makes the PIN reset required, while single_flag_escalation routes the card to the cannot-unlock options, where the reset is only one choice the customer may accept."},{"case":"Card on an account with a stolen replacement in the last 90 days","where":["check_recent_stolen","cannot_unlock_options"],"why":"check_recent_stolen offers only a transfer to a human agent, while check_unauthorized counts the card as cannot-unlock, so cannot_unlock_options also offers closure or a PIN reset."},{"case":"Score 8-10","where":["decide","unlock_handoff"],"why":"decide requires both a confirmation and a satisfactory explanation, while unlock_handoff allows the unlock for 5-10 with the customer's confirmation alone."}]}
